# Local VS Code extension updates

## Daily local debug / reinstall (default)

Do **not** bump `extensions/vscode-codelint/package.json` `version` for ordinary fixes
and UI tweaks. Rebuild and force-reinstall the same version:

```bash
cd extensions/vscode-codelint
bash scripts/install-local-vscode.sh   # or: npm run install:vscode
```

`--force` overwrites the installed extension even when the version string is unchanged.
After install, remind the user to **Reload Window** or **Restart Extensions**.

Prefer **F5 Extension Development Host** for rapid iteration when a full VSIX install
is unnecessary.

## Real releases only

Bump `version` only when the user asks to release / publish / cut a version, or when
shipping a deliberate numbered build. After a version bump, still run
`install-local-vscode.sh` so local VS Code matches.

## CLI notes

- Use `/Applications/Visual Studio Code.app/Contents/Resources/app/bin/code`
- Do **not** rely on `/usr/local/bin/code` (Cursor on this machine)
